          "name": "claims",
          "type": "value-map"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "A token whose audience names another client is refused (TOK-250).",
        "A token issued for one tenant is refused by every other (TOK-006).",
        "A token signed by a retired key is refused (TOK-251)."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The signature, audience, tenant or expiry is wrong.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "verify-identity-token",
      "name": "Verify an OpenID Connect identity token",
      "ref": "H-015",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "token",
          "type": "secret"
        },
        {
          "name": "provider",
          "type": "provider-id"
        },
        {
          "name": "nonce",
          "type": "secret"
        },
        {
          "name": "now",
          "type": "timestamp"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "subject",
          "type": "external-subject"
        },
        {
          "name": "email",
          "type": "email-address",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "name": "email-verified",
          "type": "bool"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "Only the signature method that the provider configuration names is accepted (FED-255).",
        "A signing key of one provider verifies the tokens of that provider only (FED-256)."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The issuer, audience, signature or nonce fails verification.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "verify-saml-assertion",
      "name": "Verify a SAML assertion",
      "ref": "H-016",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "response",
          "type": "bytes"
        },
        {
          "name": "provider",
          "type": "provider-id"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "subject",
          "type": "external-subject"
        },
        {
          "name": "attributes",
          "type": "value-map"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The subject and attributes come only from the assertion whose signature covers them (FED-252). The response holds exactly one assertion, a direct child of the response, with a signature of its own whose one reference is that assertion's identifier and resolves to that very element; a signed response around an unsigned assertion, a second assertion, an assertion moved elsewhere, a signature over another element and an assertion changed after it was signed are refused.",
        "The signature is checked by an XML-DSig implementation that is maintained and not written here, with the certificates of the provider's configuration only: a key or certificate that the message brings is never used, duplicate identifiers are refused and every reference digest is computed here (FED-005).",
        "The message is read with external entity and document type processing off (FED-251), at a bounded size, and an encrypted assertion, which this service cannot read, is refused and not taken for a signed one.",
        "The subject is the complete text of the name identifier, comments excluded (FED-253); an identifier that holds an element, a second identifier, an empty one or one past 255 bytes is refused.",
        "The issuer, on the assertion and on the response where it names one, is the entity identifier of the provider's configuration (FED-254).",
        "The audience of every audience restriction names this service's entity identifier at the host the sign-in started at, and the recipient of a bearer confirmation and the destination of the response, where it names one, are this host's assertion consumer address (FED-008). A condition this service does not understand is not met.",
        "The assertion is inside its validity with a skew that the configuration names (60 seconds by default): its conditions and its confirmation have an end, it is not valid before its beginning and it was not issued in the future.",
        "The response reports success, and its assertion answers the request that was made (FED-007)."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The signature, issuer, audience or recipient is wrong.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The signature, issuer, audience, recipient, destination, time or request is wrong, or the message is not one that is read.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "verify-passkey-assertion",
      "name": "Verify a passkey assertion",
      "ref": "H-017",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 3,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "assertion",
          "type": "bytes"
        },
        {
          "name": "challenge",
          "type": "challenge-id"
        },
        {
          "name": "host",
          "type": "host"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "credential",
          "type": "credential-id"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The assertion carries a challenge issued for this sign-in and bound to the address of the request (IDN-264).",
        "The relying party is the address of the tenant (IDN-007).",
        "A challenge answers once and lapses (IDN-264).",
        "An assertion whose signature counter does not go forward is refused and audited, and the credential is not used again until the person has removed it (case passkey-counter-regress).",
        "A credential is used at the address it was registered for, by the person it names."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The signature, challenge or relying party is wrong.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "verify-one-time-code",
      "name": "Verify a time-based one-time code",
      "ref": "H-018",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 3,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
