    {
      "id": "load-decision-snapshot",
      "name": "Load a snapshot with the texts functions cannot compute yet",
      "ref": "H-031",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "implementedBy": "store-contract",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "tenant",
          "type": "tenant-id"
        },
        {
          "name": "needs",
          "type": "list<need>"
        },
        {
          "name": "intent",
          "type": "intent",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "name": "mutation",
          "type": "mutation",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "name": "path",
          "type": "string",
          "optional": true
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "state",
          "type": "state"
        },
        {
          "name": "texts",
          "type": "intent-texts"
        },
        {
          "name": "segments",
          "type": "list<string>"
        },
        {
          "name": "routes",
          "type": "map<view-id, list<route-segment>>"
        },
        {
          "name": "times",
          "type": "map<string, i64>"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "state is what load-tenant (CT-012) gives for the tenant and the needs.",
        "texts holds the kernel's printing (Display of Expr) of every default and constraint of the snapshot's schema, of every policy condition under policy:<id> and of every query filter under query:<id>; blank-name is whether the name of a CreateTenant intent is blank after trimming.",
        "segments is the path split at / without empty segments; routes is the route of each view of the schema so split, a segment :name read as the parameter name; times holds each string of the mutation's fields that substrate plain.rs parse_time accepts, with its milliseconds.",
        "The hole holds the printing, the string splitting and the date parsing the function language lacks (WG-4957); when it has them, the derivations load through load-tenant and compute the rest in functions, and this hole goes."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "unavailable",
          "condition": "The store could not do the work right now (busy, I/O); safe to retry.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "unavailable"
        },
        {
          "name": "corrupt",
          "condition": "Stored data could not be read back; not safe to ignore.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "internal"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "commit-accepted",
      "name": "Commit an accepted intent",
      "ref": "CT-262",
      "realisation": "generated",
      "implementedBy": "store-contract",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "timeoutMs": 300,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "context",
          "type": "context"
        },
        {
          "name": "accepted",
          "type": "accepted-intent"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "receipt",
          "type": "receipt"
        }
      ],
      "preconditions": [
        "The base revision of the transition's delta is the revision the tenant is stored at, or the tenant is absent and the base is none."
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "Commits storage-api Commit::of(intent, context, transition) as commit-transition (CT-014) does: the delta, the events, the journal entry (with the kernel version and the hashes of the delta and the events) and the session revocations of the transition's RevokeSessions effects, all or none."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "conflict",
          "condition": "The stored revision of the tenant differs from the base revision of the delta; nothing is changed.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "conflict"
        },
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The commit is malformed, or its events do not continue the tenant event sequence without a gap; nothing is changed.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "name": "unavailable",
          "condition": "The store could not do the work right now (busy, I/O); safe to retry.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "unavailable"
        },
        {
          "name": "corrupt",
          "condition": "Stored data could not be read back; not safe to ignore.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "internal"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "mutate-record",
      "name": "Change a record of the tenant",
      "ref": "CT-263",
      "realisation": "derived",
      "implementedBy": "runtime",
      "bffRoute": "POST /api/records records",
      "derivation": {
        "kind": "command",
        "needs": "header-needs",
        "load": "load-decision-snapshot",
        "decide": "decide-mutation",
        "commit": "commit-accepted",
        "conflict": "conflict",
        "insufficient": "insufficient-state",
        "needRounds": 32,
        "retries": 8,
        "fault": "fault"
      },
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "session",
        "tenantPolicies": true,
        "csrf": true,
        "origin": true,
        "requires": [
          "content-write"
        ],
        "description": "A principal whose policies permit the change; anonymous callers carry the request token (GWY-002)"
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "timeoutMs": 10000,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "tenant",
          "type": "tenant-id",
          "description": "The tenant the host name serves, the context's."
        },
        {
          "name": "context",
          "type": "context",
          "description": "The caller's context, which the route builds from the session and the request (backend auth.rs Identity::context), not from the body."
        },
        {
          "name": "mutation",
          "type": "mutation"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "reply",
          "type": "mutation-reply",
          "optional": true,
          "description": "Present for every accepted mutation: each one creates, changes or deletes a record."
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The generic records endpoint (backend ops.rs mutate): the mutation's fields are coerced by field type, the intent is decided by the kernel against what it needs and committed atomically, as execute-intent does, and the reply names the record, its new version (none after a delete), the revision, the event sequence and the checks passed.",
        "Every publication write (create-article, update-article, delete-article, save-site-settings) is a facade lowered onto it."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "rejected",
          "condition": "The request was refused; the body is the error reply, whose code says why: not_found for no site or no object type, invalid for a field that does not coerce, and for a kernel rejection error-code-of of its kind (a refused change to a record the caller cannot read answers as unknown-record).",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "name": "insufficient-state",
          "condition": "The decision asked for more needs than needRounds allows, or for one it was already given.",
          "type": "need",
          "kind": "internal"
        },
        {
          "name": "conflict",
          "condition": "Every commit lost its race to another one, retries times over; nothing is changed.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "conflict"
        },
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The commit is malformed, or its events do not continue the tenant event sequence without a gap; nothing is changed.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "name": "unavailable",
          "condition": "The store could not do the work right now (busy, I/O); safe to retry.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "unavailable"
        },
        {
          "name": "corrupt",
          "condition": "Stored data could not be read back; not safe to ignore.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "internal"
        },
        {
          "name": "fault",
          "condition": "An integer overflow in the decision (a revision, an event sequence, a version or a record id past its type); never in practice.",
          "kind": "internal"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "public",
      "tenantScope": "request"
    },
    {
      "id": "read-view",
      "name": "Read a view of the tenant",
      "ref": "CT-264",
      "realisation": "derived",
      "implementedBy": "runtime",
      "bffRoute": "GET /api/view view",
      "derivation": {
        "kind": "read",
        "needs": "header-needs",
        "load": "load-decision-snapshot",
        "decide": "assemble-view",
        "insufficient": "insufficient-state",
        "needRounds": 32,
        "fault": "fault"
      },
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "anonymous",
        "justification": "Published views are for visitors; a session only widens what its policies let it read.",
        "requires": [
          "content-read"
        ],
        "description": "Anyone; a session widens what its policies let it read"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "timeoutMs": 10000,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "tenant",
          "type": "tenant-id",
          "description": "The tenant the host name serves, the context's."
        },
        {
          "name": "context",
          "type": "context",
          "description": "The caller's context, which the route builds from the session and the request (backend auth.rs Identity::context), not from the body."
        },
        {
          "name": "path",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "request",
          "type": "map<string, string>"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "view",
          "type": "view-data"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The generic view endpoint (backend ops.rs view): the view whose route matches the path, every section read from one snapshot through the kernel's read authorization, the rows and included records without another principal's authorship.",
        "The browser receives the view projected (project-view) by the BFF, which adds the path and, until WG-4942, the publication template's theme and desk fields.",
        "Every publication page read (read-front-page to read-lab-view) is a facade lowered onto it."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "rejected",
          "condition": "The request was refused; the body is the error reply, whose code says why: not_found for no site or no object type, invalid for a field that does not coerce, and for a kernel rejection error-code-of of its kind (a refused change to a record the caller cannot read answers as unknown-record).",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "name": "insufficient-state",
          "condition": "The decision asked for more needs than needRounds allows, or for one it was already given.",
          "type": "need",
          "kind": "internal"
        },
        {
          "name": "unavailable",
          "condition": "The store could not do the work right now (busy, I/O); safe to retry.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "unavailable"
        },
        {
          "name": "corrupt",
          "condition": "Stored data could not be read back; not safe to ignore.",
          "type": "store-error",
          "kind": "internal"
        },
        {
          "name": "fault",
          "condition": "An integer overflow in the route match (a revision, an event sequence, a version or a record id past its type); never in practice.",
          "kind": "internal"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "public",
      "tenantScope": "request",
      "readOnly": true
    },
    {
      "id": "issue-passkey-challenge",
      "name": "Issue a passkey challenge",
      "ref": "H-031",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 3,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "anonymous",
        "csrf": true,
        "origin": true,
        "justification": "A sign-in challenge is asked for before any session exists; a registration challenge additionally needs the session.",
        "requires": [
          "identity-sign-in"
        ],
        "description": "Anyone for a sign-in, a signed-in principal for a registration"
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "challenge",
          "type": "challenge-id"
        },
        {
          "name": "options",
          "type": "bytes"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The challenge is kept by the identity service with the address it was requested at and, for a registration, the session that asked; it answers once and lapses (IDN-264).",
        "A request that does not come from a host name, an address that WebAuthn can bind a passkey to, is refused."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "throttled",
          "condition": "The caller exceeded a limit that applies to it.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "throttled"
        },
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The site is not reached by a host name.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "name": "unauthenticated",
          "condition": "A registration was asked for without a valid session.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unauthenticated"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "public",
      "tenantScope": "request"
    },
    {
      "id": "list-passkeys",
