    },
    {
      "id": "deliver-sign-in-mail",
      "name": "Deliver a sign-in message through the mail transport",
      "ref": "H-034",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 3,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "to",
          "type": "email-address"
        },
        {
          "name": "subject",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "text",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "postconditions": [
        "The message goes to the mail transport, which is an SMTP server only when the operator configured one; otherwise it is the development sink, which keeps the message and sends nothing, so that no development or test run reaches a real address.",
        "A transport that talks to a server delivers off the caller's thread and logs a delivery that fails, so that how long the call takes and whether it fails say nothing about whether the address has an account (IDN-006).",
        "The message carries the sign-in link, whose token is in the fragment of its address (D-703) and whose challenge holds the principal and no email address (PRV-365)."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "unavailable",
          "condition": "The transport did not accept the message.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unavailable"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "check-return-address",
      "name": "Check a return address",
      "ref": "H-035",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 3,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "next",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "path",
          "type": "string",
          "optional": true
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The result is the address itself when it is a path on the host of the tenant: it starts with one slash, names no other host, holds no backslash and no control character, and is not longer than 512 bytes (FED-250).",
        "Any other address gives no result, and the person lands on the default page instead of being sent on.",
        "A sign-in link carries a return address only when this check passes, and the page that the link opens checks it again before it navigates."
      ],
      "errors": [],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "configure-identity-providers",
      "name": "Configure the identity providers of a tenant",
      "ref": "H-036",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "roles": [
          "platform-operator"
        ],
        "description": "Platform operator, through the platform configuration file and the process environment"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "tenant",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "provider",
          "type": "provider-id"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "postconditions": [
        "A tenant's identity providers are platform configuration and not tenant data: one file that the operator names (STRATA_OIDC_CONFIG) maps each tenant to its providers. A tenant's own people cannot change who is let in by a provider, and the operator, who holds the client secret, can.",
        "A provider names an identifier of 1 to 32 lower-case letters, digits and hyphens, a label for the sign-in page, its issuer and client identifier, the signature methods its tokens may use (RS256, ES256 and EdDSA, and never none or a shared-secret method, FED-255), the email domains it decides for, whether a first sign-in creates a principal (FED-011) and the one default role that principal receives (FED-258).",
        "The client secret is never in the file: the file names an environment variable that holds it. The secret is read when the process starts, kept in a value that does not print, sent only to the provider's token endpoint and written to no log, audit entry or reply. A name that is not set stops the process from starting.",
        "A provider that is not enabled is offered on no sign-in page, cannot be started, accepts no callback and binds none of its domains (FED-011).",
        "The sign-in page offers the enabled providers of the realm of the address it is served at, and no other realm's (FED-010).",
        "Provider metadata and keys are held per provider of a tenant and never shared between providers (FED-256)."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The file does not parse, names a signature method that is not allowed, a provider twice, or an environment variable that is not set.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "redeem-oidc-code",
      "name": "Redeem an authorization code and check the identity token",
      "ref": "H-037",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; the client secret goes to the provider's token endpoint only"
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "state",
          "type": "secret"
        },
        {
          "name": "code",
          "type": "secret"
        },
        {
          "name": "binding",
          "type": "secret"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "subject",
          "type": "external-subject"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "A pending request holds the nonce, the proof-key verifier and the hash of the nonce kept in the starting browser's cookie, found by the hash of its state value. It is taken out of the store in the step that reads it, so a callback answers once, and it is accepted only through its lifetime, from the browser that started it and at the address it started at (FED-001).",
        "The authorization request carries a state value, a nonce and the S256 challenge of a verifier, and the redirect address is the callback path of the host of the tenant (FED-002). The code is redeemed with that verifier.",
        "Metadata that names another issuer than the one configured is not used, and neither is an address that is not HTTPS (HTTP is allowed in development only). A fetch follows no redirect, times out and reads a bounded answer.",
        "The identity token is checked as verify-identity-token states, with the keys of that provider: algorithm allowlist, issuer, audience, authorised party, expiry and issue time with a skew of 60 seconds, subject and nonce (FED-003, FED-255).",
        "A token that names a key that is not held makes the provider's keys be fetched once more and is checked again; a key that is still not there is a refusal, and a second fetch is not made within 30 seconds of the last, so that made-up key names cannot make this process fetch without end (FED-004).",
        "A provider that does not answer refuses its own callbacks and its own starts, and leaves every other way in the realm has usable (FED-013).",
        "Every refusal says the same to the person, whatever failed; the reason is in the log and holds no token, code, state or address."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "unauthenticated",
          "condition": "The state matches no pending request of this browser, the code does not redeem, or the token fails a check.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unauthenticated"
        },
        {
          "name": "unavailable",
          "condition": "The provider's metadata cannot be fetched when a sign-in starts.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unavailable"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "refuse-bound-domain-sign-in",
      "name": "Refuse password and emailed-link sign-in in a provider-bound domain",
      "ref": "H-038",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "address",
          "type": "email-address"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "bound",
          "type": "bool"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "An address is in a bound domain when its part after the last @, in lower case, is one of the domains of an enabled provider of the realm, of either protocol (FED-009). A provider that is not enabled binds nothing, so that disabling it is how a realm lifts the binding.",
        "A password for such an address is refused as a wrong password is, after the same work, so that neither the answer nor its time says that the domain is bound (IDN-255).",
        "A request for an emailed link for such an address is answered as one for an address with no account is, and no message is sent (IDN-006).",
        "A login with no @ is in no bound domain."
      ],
      "errors": [],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "resolve-federated-identity",
      "name": "Decide whose account a verified identity is",
      "ref": "H-039",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "description": "Local call inside the platform process; no network credential"
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "provider",
          "type": "provider-id"
        },
        {
          "name": "subject",
          "type": "external-subject"
        },
        {
          "name": "email",
          "type": "email-address",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "name": "email-verified",
          "type": "bool"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "principal",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "An identity is a provider of the realm and the provider's subject identifier. It is tied to one principal, once; a subject of one provider is never another provider's (FED-256).",
        "A known identity signs its principal in. A first sign-in never takes the account of another person: an identity is linked to an existing principal only after that principal has signed in and asked to link, and the callback of that request answers only to the session that asked (FED-012).",
        "Where the realm decided to trust a provider that far, and only then, an address that the provider marks as verified links to the account whose login is that address. An address that is not marked verified links to nothing. By default no address links to anything (FED-257).",
        "A first sign-in creates a principal only when the realm enabled creation (FED-011). A realm that restricted the provider to domains lets in only a verified address in one of them.",
        "The principal created has a login that no password opens, holds the one default role that the realm names and no other, and its name is made from the realm, the provider and the subject, so that two first sign-ins that arrive together make one (FED-258).",
        "A principal created and an identity linked are audit entries; the entry names the principal and the provider, and no address.",
        "The same decision serves every protocol: a provider of the realm is an OpenID Connect or a SAML provider, a principal's name and login are made from the protocol as well as the realm, the provider and the subject, and the audit entries of a created principal and a linked identity name the protocol."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "unauthenticated",
          "condition": "The realm does not admit the identity.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unauthenticated"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "configure-saml-providers",
      "name": "Configure the SAML providers of a tenant",
      "ref": "H-050",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "in-process",
        "roles": [
          "platform-operator"
        ],
        "description": "Platform operator, through the platform configuration file"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "tenant",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "name": "provider",
          "type": "provider-id"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "postconditions": [
        "A tenant's SAML providers are platform configuration and not tenant data, as its OpenID Connect providers are: one file that the operator names (STRATA_SAML_CONFIG) maps each tenant to its providers. A tenant's own people cannot change who is let in by a provider, and the operator can.",
        "A provider names an identifier of 1 to 32 lower-case letters, digits and hyphens, a label for the sign-in page, the entity identifier its assertions are issued under (FED-254), the address of its sign-on service, and one to four certificates in PEM that it signs with (FED-005), given inline or as files that are read when the process starts. Several certificates are for a rotation: an assertion signed by any one of them is the provider's.",
        "A certificate that cannot be read, a sign-on address that is not HTTPS (HTTP is allowed in development only) or holds credentials, a skew outside 0 to 300 seconds and a provider named twice stop the process from starting. There is no secret in the file.",
        "The entity identifier of this service for a provider is the one the file names, and otherwise the address of the provider's metadata at the host the sign-in started at, so that each host of the platform is a service provider of its own and an assertion issued for another host's is refused (FED-008).",
        "A provider that is not enabled is offered on no sign-in page, cannot be started, accepts no response, has no metadata and binds none of its domains (FED-009, FED-011). Its domains, its first-sign-in creation, its default role and its link by address are those of an OpenID Connect provider and are decided in the same place (H-039).",
        "An address the provider sends is treated as verified only where the operator says the provider checks addresses (email_verified): only then does it bind a domain at a first sign-in (FED-009) or link an account (FED-257)."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The file does not parse, a certificate or an address in it is not usable, or a provider appears twice.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "local"
    },
    {
      "id": "start-saml-sign-in",
      "name": "Start a sign-in at a SAML provider",
      "ref": "H-051",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "anonymous",
        "csrf": true,
        "origin": true,
        "justification": "Signing in with a provider starts before any session exists.",
        "requires": [
          "identity-sign-in"
        ],
        "description": "Anyone from one of the site's own pages, with the request token every sign-in carries; to link a provider to an account, the signed-in person"
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "provider",
          "type": "provider-id"
        },
        {
          "name": "next",
          "type": "string",
          "optional": true
        },
        {
          "name": "link",
          "type": "bool",
          "optional": true
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "redirect",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "A sign-in at a SAML provider starts at this service and only here: a response is accepted only for a request this service made (FED-007, D-8). Sign-in started by the provider is not offered; a tenant that has not turned it on has none, and none can be turned on in this release.",
        "The authentication request names this service by its entity identifier, the provider's sign-on address as its destination, the assertion consumer address of the host the sign-in started at, and the POST binding for the response. It is sent as the HTTP-Redirect binding: raw DEFLATE, base64, and a relay state, in the query of the provider's sign-on address.",
        "A pending request is kept, found by the hash of the relay state, holding the identifier of the authentication request, the provider, the hash of a binding nonce, the address the sign-in started at, and the principal that was signed in when the person asked to link. The relay state and the identifier are random, and the relay state is in no log, audit entry or reply but the one that goes to the provider.",
        "The binding nonce goes to the starting browser as a `__Host-` cookie, `Strict`, that the page cannot read, and is in no address. The return address is kept only when it is a path on the site (FED-250).",
        "Starting is counted against the source and the realm and not against the provider, so that a few clicks of anyone's do not close the provider's button for everyone.",
        "Metadata for the provider is served at the host the person asked at: this service's entity identifier, the one assertion consumer address, the POST binding, and that assertions are to be signed. It holds nothing secret and is not found for a provider that does not exist, is not enabled or is another site's."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The provider does not exist or is not enabled.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "name": "forbidden",
          "condition": "The request did not come from one of the site's own pages.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "forbidden"
        },
        {
          "name": "unauthenticated",
          "condition": "A request to link was made by no one who is signed in.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unauthenticated"
        },
        {
          "name": "unavailable",
          "condition": "The provider's sign-on address is not one the browser may be sent to.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unavailable"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "public",
      "tenantScope": "request"
    },
    {
      "id": "carry-saml-response-to-sign-in-page",
      "name": "Carry a SAML response from the provider's post to the sign-in page",
      "ref": "H-053",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "anonymous",
        "justification": "The provider's page posts from another site and carries no session; it only carries the response on to the sign-in page, which checks it.",
        "requires": [
          "identity-sign-in"
        ],
        "description": "Anyone: the provider's page posts from another site and carries no session"
      },
      "idempotent": true,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "response",
          "type": "secret"
        },
        {
          "name": "relay-state",
          "type": "secret"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "location",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The assertion consumer address takes the provider's POST and signs no one in. It reads the form, moves the response and the relay state into the fragment of the sign-in page's address, which the browser sends nowhere, and answers with a redirect to it. The page takes them out of the address bar and sends them in the body of one request from the site's own origin, with the request token every sign-in carries and with the binding cookie, which is `Strict` and so does not accompany the provider's post.",
        "A form that carries no base64 response, one past 48 KiB of base64, or a relay state that is not one this service makes sends the page to say that the provider did not sign the person in, and nothing else is read from it.",
        "The return address of the sign-in is a cookie that holds a path on the site and nothing secret. It is `SameSite=None`, because the way back is a POST, which a `Lax` cookie does not accompany; it is read only as a path on the site (FED-250) and is cleared by this answer.",
        "The address is answered at the hosts the platform serves and no other."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "not-found",
          "condition": "No site is served at the address.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "not_found"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "public",
      "tenantScope": "request",
      "readOnly": true
    },
    {
      "id": "consume-saml-response",
      "name": "Check a SAML response and its assertion, once",
      "ref": "H-052",
      "realisation": "hand",
      "milestone": 4,
      "implementedBy": "identity-service",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "anonymous",
        "csrf": true,
        "origin": true,
        "justification": "Signing in with a provider happens before any session exists; the signed assertion proves the identity.",
        "requires": [
          "identity-federate"
        ],
        "description": "Anyone from one of the site's own pages, with the request token every sign-in carries"
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "relay-state",
          "type": "secret"
        },
        {
          "name": "response",
          "type": "secret"
        },
        {
          "name": "binding",
          "type": "secret"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "subject",
          "type": "external-subject"
        }
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The pending request is taken out of the store in the step that reads it, so a response answers once whatever follows, and it is accepted only through its lifetime, from the browser whose cookie holds the binding nonce and at the address it started at (FED-007). A response that answers no pending request is refused.",
        "The assertion is checked as verify-saml-assertion states, against the provider's certificates and this host's entity identifier and assertion consumer address, and it must answer the request that was made (InResponseTo, on the assertion's confirmation and on the response where it names one).",
        "The identifier of an assertion that passed every check is remembered, by hash, for the provider of the tenant, until it would no longer be accepted anyway (its end plus the skew), in the one step that also says whether it was already there. A second presentation, in any browser and at any time inside that window, is refused (FED-006). A message that is refused does not use its identifier up.",
        "What the verified identity means for the realm is decided by resolve-federated-identity: the same for a SAML provider as for an OpenID Connect one.",
        "Every refusal says the same to the person, whatever failed; the reason is in the log and holds no response, assertion, relay state, address or identifier. The attempt is limited like every other sign-in method's."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "unauthenticated",
          "condition": "The response answers no pending request of this browser, or the assertion fails a check, or it was presented before.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unauthenticated"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "public",
      "tenantScope": "request"
    },
    {
      "id": "assign-role",
      "name": "Give a person a role",
      "ref": "CT-265",
      "realisation": "generated",
      "implementedBy": "gateway",
      "bffRoute": "POST /api/members/assign-role",
      "auth": {
        "scheme": "session",
        "tenantPolicies": true,
        "csrf": true,
        "origin": true,
        "description": "A signed-in person whose tenant policies let them manage members",
        "requires": [
          "members-manage"
        ]
      },
      "idempotent": false,
      "timeoutMs": 10000,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "principal",
          "type": "principal-id"
        },
        {
          "name": "role",
          "type": "role-id"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "revision",
          "type": "u64"
        },
        {
          "name": "event-seq",
          "type": "u64"
        }
      ],
      "preconditions": [
        "The request carries the request token of the session (GWY-002)."
      ],
      "postconditions": [
        "The person holds the role, directly, when the call is accepted (ADM-150).",
        "The call is refused unless the caller holds every permission and capability the role grants; the owner holds all of them, and only an owner confers owner (ADM-152)."
      ],
      "errors": [
        {
          "name": "unauthenticated",
          "condition": "No valid session or credential accompanies the request.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unauthenticated"
        },
        {
          "name": "forbidden",
          "condition": "The caller may not manage members, or the role is one whose permissions and capabilities the caller does not hold in full; the failed check names the role (ADM-152).",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "forbidden"
        },
        {
          "name": "invalid",
          "condition": "The role is unknown, or it is public, which everyone holds.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "invalid"
        },
        {
          "name": "unavailable",
          "condition": "A dependency of the operation did not answer.",
          "type": "api-error",
          "kind": "unavailable"
        }
      ],
      "exposure": "public",
      "tenantScope": "request"
    },
