    {"id":"sec-platform-5","title":"Assurance","level":2,"document":"doc-platform","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:asr-001}}\n\n{{entity:asr-002}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-9","title":"Architecture review","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":101,"body":"\nThe goals, constraints, decisions, boundaries, components and open questions that the architecture review adds. The requirements that trace to them are in [architecture](../09-architecture/architecture.md).\n\n**Goals**\n\n{{entity:g-100}}\n{{entity:g-101}}\n{{entity:g-102}}\n{{entity:g-103}}\n{{entity:g-104}}\n\n**Constraints**\n\n{{entity:k-100}}\n\n**Decisions**\n\n{{entity:d-100}}\n{{entity:d-101}}\n{{entity:d-102}}\n{{entity:d-103}}\n\n**Boundaries**\n\n{{entity:b-100}}\n{{entity:b-101}}\n\n**Components**\n\n{{entity:limit-store}}\n{{entity:backup-archive}}\n{{entity:fleet-reporting}}\n{{entity:product-module}}\n{{entity:external-endpoint}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-209","title":"Conversational interface review","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":209,"body":"\nThe conversational interface and the authoring experience, seen from the person at the screen.\n\n**Goals**\n\n{{entity:g-200}}\n{{entity:g-201}}\n{{entity:g-202}}\n{{entity:g-203}}\n{{entity:g-204}}\n{{entity:g-205}}\n{{entity:g-206}}\n{{entity:g-207}}\n\n**Non-goals**\n\n{{entity:ng-200}}\n{{entity:ng-201}}\n{{entity:ng-202}}\n\n**Boundaries**\n\n{{entity:b-200}}\n{{entity:b-201}}\n{{entity:b-202}}\n\n**Components**\n\n{{entity:conversation-service}}\n{{entity:model-provider}}\n{{entity:local-model-adapter}}\n\n**Decisions**\n\n{{entity:d-200}}\n{{entity:d-201}}\n{{entity:d-202}}\n{{entity:d-203}}\n{{entity:d-204}}\n{{entity:d-205}}\n\n**Constraints**\n\n{{entity:k-200}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-1","title":"Architecture","level":1,"document":"doc-architecture","order":1,"body":"\nThe requirements that the component model has to support and that the other documents do not state: what the platform does while the control plane is down, how notices and outbox events are delivered, how formats change while two versions run, how much one decision loads, which limits are shared, how tenants are backed up, and how a product module is added. Each requirement names the boundary it is observed at and the components that carry it.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-2","title":"Control plane and wake index","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-100}}\n\n{{entity:arc-101}}\n\n{{entity:arc-500}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-3","title":"Notices and outbox","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-102}}\n\n{{entity:arc-103}}\n\n{{entity:arc-104}}\n\n{{entity:arc-105}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-4","title":"Change across versions","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-106}}\n\n{{entity:arc-107}}\n\n{{entity:arc-115}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-5","title":"Kernel load, limits and connections","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-108}}\n\n{{entity:arc-109}}\n\n{{entity:arc-114}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-6","title":"Reporting and backup","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":6,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-110}}\n\n{{entity:arc-111}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-7","title":"Extension","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":7,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-112}}\n\n{{entity:arc-113}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-index-1","title":"Specification","level":1,"document":"doc-index","order":1,"body":"\nRequirements derived from [the white paper](00-vision/whitepaper.md), in the format Concordance lints. Each one names the boundary it is observed at, what it traces to, how it is proved and the milestone at which it is first verified. Case tables live beside their file, in `cases/`.\n\n| File | Prefix | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| [01-core/kernel.md](01-core/kernel.md) | KRN | The pure transition function, its invariants and the abstract model |\n| [01-core/storage.md](01-core/storage.md) | STO | The store contract and its adapters |\n| [01-core/runtime.md](01-core/runtime.md) | RUN, GWY, SIM | What the existing services and the simulator guarantee today |\n| [02-tenancy/tenancy.md](02-tenancy/tenancy.md) | TEN | The control plane, the tenant directory and the life of a tenant |\n| [03-identity/identity.md](03-identity/identity.md) | IDN | Realms, sign-in methods, sessions, factors and recovery |\n| [03-identity/federation.md](03-identity/federation.md) | FED | OpenID Connect, SAML and SCIM |\n| [03-identity/tokens.md](03-identity/tokens.md) | TOK | Service accounts, agent identities, delegation and signing keys |\n| [04-automation/scheduling.md](04-automation/scheduling.md) | SCH | Jobs, schedules, triggers and leases |\n| [04-automation/workflows.md](04-automation/workflows.md) | WFL | Workflows as metadata, connectors and scheduled publication |\n| [05-delivery/copies.md](05-delivery/copies.md) | CPY | How data is kept outside its owner for cheaper reads, and how it stays right |\n| [05-delivery/edge.md](05-delivery/edge.md) | EDG | The content delivery network, domains, certificates and limits |\n| [06-agents/operations.md](06-agents/operations.md) | AGT | The operation catalogue, dry runs, proposals and limits on agents |\n| [06-agents/observability.md](06-agents/observability.md) | OBS | Telemetry, correlation, health and the audit log |\n| [06-agents/safety.md](06-agents/safety.md) | AGS | Agent safety and governance: untrusted text, delegation, blast radius, platform-operating agents, data leaving the platform and concurrent change |\n| [07-content/content.md](07-content/content.md) | CMS | Content types, versions, media, languages and preview |\n| [08-platform/platform.md](08-platform/platform.md) | DEP, SEC, ASR | The local stack, the cloud profile, keys and the assurance loop |\n| [09-privacy/privacy.md](09-privacy/privacy.md) | PRV | Data subject rights, sealing, retention and legal hold, residency, consent, platform access and compliance evidence |\n| [09-operations/reliability.md](09-operations/reliability.md) | OPS | Reference load, admission, retries, failure containment, data safety, releases, objectives, alerts and runbooks |\n| [09-threat/threat-model.md](09-threat/threat-model.md) | THR | The attack classes that cut across components: response headers, transport, reachability, supply chain, incidents and abuse |\n| [09-conversation/conversation.md](09-conversation/conversation.md) | CNV | The conversational interface: the assistant, previews and confirmations, explanations, the model provider and onboarding |\n| [09-conversation/authoring.md](09-conversation/authoring.md) | UXA | Empty, failing, unsaved, shared and expired states of the authoring application and sign-in pages, and reader throttling |\n| [09-administration/administration.md](09-administration/administration.md) | ADM | Roles, teams, invitations, sandbox and staging tenants, offboarding and support access |\n| [02-tenancy/billing.md](02-tenancy/billing.md) | BIL | Plans, quotas, trials, metering, the billing export and published objectives |\n| [04-automation/notifications.md](04-automation/notifications.md) | NTF | Subscriptions, email and inbox notices, approval tasks |\n| [04-automation/integrations.md](04-automation/integrations.md) | INT | Inbound and outbound webhooks, the trigger and action catalogue, installed templates |\n| [07-content/forms.md](07-content/forms.md) | FRM | Form submissions: storage, tokens, notices, retention and export |\n| [07-content/search.md](07-content/search.md) | SRH | Search over published and draft content, limited by audience |\n| [09-architecture/architecture.md](09-architecture/architecture.md) | ARC, H | The control plane's availability, notices and outbox, change across versions, kernel load, shared limits, reporting, backup and extension |\n| [07-content/content-tokens.md](07-content/content-tokens.md) | CTK | Tenant-defined tokens: definition, evaluation, output contexts, stored copies and email |\n| [04-automation/email.md](04-automation/email.md) | EML | The mail contract and its adapters, sending, sender domains, suppression and the mail log |\n| [02-tenancy/tenant-migrations.md](02-tenancy/tenant-migrations.md) | MIG | Tenant migrations: the guarantee a tenant keeps through its own changes, platform changes and moves, the conversions, imports and exports that carry them |\n| [08-platform/release-lifecycle.md](08-platform/release-lifecycle.md) | REL | Release lifecycle: image digests, stage and production environments and parity, promotion and approval, colour switches, rollback and the release records |\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-150","title":"Product review","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":150,"body":"\nWhat a customer can buy, what the first release left out, and the decisions that follow from it.\n\n**Goals**\n\n{{entity:g-150}}\n\n{{entity:g-151}}\n\n{{entity:g-152}}\n\n{{entity:g-153}}\n\n{{entity:g-154}}\n\n{{entity:g-155}}\n\n{{entity:g-156}}\n\n{{entity:g-157}}\n\n{{entity:g-158}}\n\n{{entity:g-159}}\n\n{{entity:g-160}}\n\n{{entity:g-161}}\n\n{{entity:g-162}}\n\n{{entity:g-163}}\n\n{{entity:g-164}}\n\n{{entity:g-165}}\n\n{{entity:g-166}}\n\n{{entity:g-167}}\n\n{{entity:g-168}}\n\n**Non-goals**\n\n{{entity:ng-150}}\n\n{{entity:ng-151}}\n\n{{entity:ng-152}}\n\n{{entity:ng-153}}\n\n{{entity:ng-154}}\n\n{{entity:ng-155}}\n\n**Boundaries**\n\n{{entity:b-150}}\n\n{{entity:b-151}}\n\n{{entity:b-152}}\n\n{{entity:b-153}}\n\n{{entity:b-154}}\n\n{{entity:b-155}}\n\n{{entity:b-156}}\n\n**Decisions**\n\n{{entity:d-150}}\n\n{{entity:d-151}}\n\n{{entity:d-152}}\n\n{{entity:d-153}}\n\n{{entity:d-154}}\n\n**Components**\n\n{{entity:search-index}}\n\n{{entity:notification-service}}\n\n"},
