    {
      "id": "needs",
      "description": "transition.rs needs, the pure body of contract plan-intent-needs (CT-002): the state an intent is expected to need, which the shell loads before deciding it (a plan; decide-intent guards every lookup itself). None without a schema; nothing for CreateTenant and the role intents; the field needs of a create; the record and its field needs for an update; the record and every referrer's ByField of a reference to it for a delete; every record of each touched object type for a schema change. Each once, in order (need-order).",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "schema",
          "type": "option<tenant-schema>"
        },
        {
          "name": "intent",
          "type": "intent"
        }
      ],
      "returns": "list<need>",
      "body": "match schema { None => [], Some(s) => call need-order(match intent { create-tenant => [], assign-role => [], revoke-role => [], create-record{object, fields} => call field-needs(s, object, fields), update-record{object, id, fields} => concat([need.record{object, id}], call field-needs(s, object, fields)), delete-record{object, id} => concat([need.record{object, id}], map(rf in call referrers(s, object), need.by-field{object: rf.object.id, field: rf.field.id, value: value.ref(id)})), change-schema{changes} => map(o in call touched-objects(changes), need.all-of(o)) }) }",
      "examples": [
        {
          "description": "behaviour.rs a_thin_snapshot_is_refused_with_the_missing_need: the uniqueness lookup.",
